abstract:
The Continuum Hypothesis implies an Erd"os-Sierpi'nski like duality between the ideal of first category subsets of $eals^{
aturals}$, and the ideal of countable dimensional subsets of $eals^{
aturals}$. The algebraic sum of a Hurewicz subset - a dimension theoretic analogue of Sierpinski sets and Lusin sets - of $eals^{
aturals}$ with any compactly countable dimensional subset of $eals^{
aturals}$ has first category.
